UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 40, Lesson 2: Portfolio selection and reflection', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Portfolio selection means choosing pieces that show progress and explaining why each piece matters, plus a forward goal.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same strategy to an unfamiliar topic or audience, then compare the effect of two different choices.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nName two pieces to keep and one sentence why for each.\n\nFEEDBACK\nWhy must link to a skill improvement, not only \"I like it\".\n\nCHECK\nA pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nSelect four pieces across reading, writing and speaking/handwriting. Write a why for each and one overall goal. Share one selection aloud.\n\nWrite a short reflection describing one specific revision you made and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"English","learning_intention":"Portfolio selection means choosing pieces that show progress and explaining why each piece matters, plus a forward goal.","lesson_number":2,"lesson_role":"Writing","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN2-CWT-02"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Select four pieces across reading, writing and speaking/handwriting. Write a why for each and one overall goal. Share one selection aloud. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: original example using portfolio on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample error: A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection.. Correction: Why must link to a skill improvement, not only \"I like it\".. Why it helps the audience is stated.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating portfolio on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with portfolio, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept original work about portfolio with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material. / Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for portfolio. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for portfolio. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["A method that skips the key step taught in this lesson","Why must link to a skill improvement, not only \"I like it\"","A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection","A claim that names no evidence from the lesson material"],"question":"Name two pieces to keep and one sentence why for each. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for portfolio; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Why must link to a skill improvement, not only \"I like it\"","Careful use of select and explain why it matters with clear evidence","A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection","Portfolio selection means choosing pieces that show progress and explaining why each piece matters, plus a forward goal"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with portfolio?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named select and explain why it matters, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Apply portfolio to new material and name the select and explain why it matters used","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence","A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection","Name select and explain why it matters only, without linking it to portfolio"],"question":"Which response best applies portfolio with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The skill is shown by quoting or pointing to wording that carries portfolio. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Say the writing is good without naming any words","A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection","Point to exact words in the sentence that show portfolio and say what they do","Ignore the sentence and invent a more exciting event"],"question":"Read: \"After the blackout, Tess lit a candle and read the crumpled note.\" Which choice best uses portfolio from this lesson?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the language skill with textual evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged","Name select and explain why it matters without linking it to any words in the text","Why must link to a skill improvement, not only \"I like it\""],"question":"Which statement correctly applies the lesson idea about portfolio?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Start from a specific textual clue, then explain its effect. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged","Lengthen the answer with adjectives while keeping the same idea","Locate a specific word, phrase or structural clue before deciding","Guess from the title alone with no textual clue"],"question":"In a new text, what should you do first to analyse select and explain why it matters?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Repair means fixing meaning or evidence, not padding. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Delete the evidence that disagreed with your first guess","Change the inaccurate idea or missing evidence, not only the length","Add adjectives without fixing the wrong idea","Make the answer longer while keeping the same mistake"],"question":"Which revision actually improves meaning for portfolio?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Accurate transfer needs fresh material with an explained language choice. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Use a fresh sentence or text and explain one precise choice about portfolio","Retype the worked model as the final answer","Change fonts and claim the work is new","A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection"],"question":"Which response shows accurate use of portfolio on fresh material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about portfolio with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating portfolio on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using portfolio on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for portfolio. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea.","question":"Name one likely error with portfolio, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Sample error: A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection.. Correction: Why must link to a skill improvement, not only \"I like it\".. Why it helps the audience is stated.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent task and reflection, with explanations where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-eng-y3-w40-l2","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA alignment; verify content points before acceptance.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise portfolio.","Read the mission before you start writing or speaking.","Keep the audience and purpose in mind as you work."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your reason with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the evidence."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the wording that carries the meaning.","Then explain the choice without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore the example.","Prefer evidence over wording that merely sounds clever."],"submit":["Check that your response and reason are both present.","Proofread names, sequence and punctuation.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact word or action before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and underline one useful detail.","Say what that detail helps a reader understand.","A vague compliment is weaker than quoted evidence."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with a stronger revision.","Change meaning or accuracy, not only length.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh topic that still uses the same skill.","Explain one decision in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include an original response and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new content."]},"subject":"English","success_criteria":["I can use portfolio with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify select and explain why it matters.","I can practise why independently on a new prompt.","I can notice goal needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Portfolio selection means choosing pieces that show progress and explaining why each piece matters, plus a forward goal.","options":["A guess with no explanation","A claim unrelated to the text","Portfolio selection means choosing pieces that show progress and explaining why each piece matters, plus a forward goal","An answer copied without understanding"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about portfolio with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nSelected: theme paragraph (better evidence), bee report (sources listed), speech cue cards (clearer pace). Goal: stronger conclusions.\n\nTRY FIRST\nName two pieces to keep and one sentence why for each.\n\nFEEDBACK\nWhy must link to a skill improvement, not only \"I like it\".","explain":"Portfolio selection means choosing pieces that show progress and explaining why each piece matters, plus a forward goal.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"A pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Portfolio pieces chosen with skill-based reasons.","caption":"Why must name improvement.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Select</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">theme paragraph; bee report; cue cards</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Why</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">evidence; sources; pace</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Selected: theme paragraph (better evidence), bee report (sources listed), speech cue cards (clearer pace). Goal: stronge Then write your own attempt.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.\nJuno: Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: Selected: theme paragraph (better evidence), bee report (sources listed), speech cue cards (clearer pace). Goal: stronge Then write your own attempt."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.","options":["Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does","A claim unrelated to the text","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no explanation"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about portfolio with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nSelected: theme paragraph (better evidence), bee report (sources listed), speech cue cards (clearer pace). Goal: stronger conclusions. Think about how this word or relationship creates meaning.\n\nTRY FIRST\nUnderline or quote one precise detail in the model and explain its effect.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning.","explain":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Saying a choice is good without naming the actual detail does not show understanding. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Explain the evidence","visual":[{"alt":"Forward goal contrasted with an unexplained pile.","caption":"Selection plus reflection.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Goal</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">stronger conclusions</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Not portfolio</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">pile with no reasons</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison.","options":["Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison","A claim unrelated to the text","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no explanation"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about portfolio with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nA pile without reasons is not a portfolio reflection. Here is a more productive model: Selected: theme paragraph (better evidence), bee report (sources listed), speech cue cards (clearer pace). Goal: stronger conclusions.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against approach would weaken your work, then write a corrected version.\n\nFEEDBACK\nWhy must link to a skill improvement, not only \"I like it\".","explain":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific error, then show how a revision fixes that error.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choic